  "_comment": "APP MODE (plan row 0e). ComfyUI's app view shows a workflow as a form: extra.linearData.inputs is the form, top to bottom, in exactly this order (the frontend does not sort it), and extra.linearMode opens the workflow straight into it. ONE FORM FOR EVERY GENERATED WORKFLOW, in the operator's order (2026-09-26, after seeing the story-only form live: \"story, models, My Story at the bottom\"): the story rows (the bank first), then every model picker grouped by role -- writer, announcer, characters, music, each still under its video, the upscaler, then the cloud writer slots -- then the My Story rows, then Space saver. Wording and grouping from a Fable design pass the operator asked for; the form has no section headers, so the role prefixes in `labels` do that job. Per-machine workflows OPEN ON THE GRAPH (operator: graph view) and switch to the form with the App button; workflows/otr_app.json opens as the app. scripts/build_variants.py resolves each entry's node TYPE and widget against the workflow's own node ids and refuses a type that is missing or not unique, or a widget that node does not have. The canonical carries neither: it is the workflow the operator edits on the canvas. HAND-ORDERED ON PURPOSE -- the matrix's key_indicators omit the cloud slots and include machine tuning; tests/test_app_mode.py checks no matrix user-choice key is missing. `labels` gives each row a plain-English name, written as the widget input's `label` on the generated workflows only.",
